Applied by ../prep.common to upstream's src/scanner.c on every regen.
Regen fails if this patch no longer applies. If upstream has fixed the bug,
delete this file.

SECENG-77: create() allocates zero bytes with calloc(0, ...) and the scanner
then reads and writes the 4-byte state through that pointer. Fixed upstream in
alex-pinkus/tree-sitter-swift@8abb3e8b3325, which is newer than our pin.

--- a/scanner.c
+++ b/scanner.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
 };
 
 void *tree_sitter_swift_external_scanner_create() {
-    return calloc(0, sizeof(struct ScannerState));
+    return calloc(1, sizeof(struct ScannerState));
 }
 
 void tree_sitter_swift_external_scanner_destroy(void *payload) {
